# Week 10 Implementation - Capture Tools & Replay Scripts ✅

## 🎯 What Was the Point?

The Week 10 task was about creating **testing infrastructure** for your exam cheat detection system. Here's why this is important:

### Problems It Solves

1. **Manual Testing is Tedious** 
   - Before: You had to sit in front of your webcam and manually perform suspicious behaviors every time you wanted to test
   - Now: Record once, replay unlimited times

2. **Inconsistent Testing**
   - Before: Hard to reproduce exact same scenario for debugging
   - Now: Same video produces same results every time

3. **No Performance Metrics**
   - Before: No way to measure if your optimizations actually improved speed
   - Now: Detailed performance reports for every test run

4. **Difficult Debugging**
   - Before: Bugs happen in real-time and you can't go back
   - Now: Pause, replay, and analyze frame-by-frame

5. **No Regression Testing**
   - Before: New changes might break existing functionality without you knowing
   - Now: Run test suite to verify everything still works

---

## 📦 What Was Implemented

### 1. Video Capture Tool ([tools/video_capture.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/tools/video_capture.py))

**Purpose:** Record test videos with annotations

**Features:**
- ✅ Live webcam recording with preview
- ✅ Real-time annotation system (mark suspicious behaviors)
- ✅ Metadata generation (timestamps, scenario info)
- ✅ Configurable resolution and FPS
- ✅ Multiple annotation types (phone usage, head turning, etc.)

**Example Usage:**
```bash
# Record a phone usage scenario
python tools/video_capture.py --scenario phone_usage --description "Student using phone"

# Custom resolution
python tools/video_capture.py --scenario test --resolution 1920x1080 --fps 30
```

**Controls:**
- **SPACE** - Start/Stop recording
- **a** - Add annotation
- **n/p** - Next/Previous annotation type
- **q** - Quit

---

### 2. Video Replay Script ([tools/video_replay.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/tools/video_replay.py))

**Purpose:** Process recorded videos through detection pipeline

**Features:**
- ✅ Single video processing
- ✅ Batch processing (entire directory)
- ✅ Performance metrics (FPS, processing time)
- ✅ Detection statistics (suspicion scores, flagged frames)
- ✅ Annotated output videos
- ✅ JSON reports for analysis
- ✅ Live preview option

**Example Usage:**
```bash
# Process single video
python tools/video_replay.py data/test_videos/phone_usage_20250121_143022.mp4

# Process with preview
python tools/video_replay.py video.mp4 --preview

# Batch process all videos
python tools/video_replay.py data/test_videos --batch --report results.json

# Disable pose detection for speed testing
python tools/video_replay.py video.mp4 --no-pose
```

---

